Looking at the execution trace and failure analysis:

**Root cause:** The agent found Christopher Burch's conversation and even parsed movies by director (computing `fincher_movies`), but never went back to read the FULL conversation thread to understand what Christopher specifically requested. It sent all 14 movies instead of only those by the requested director.

**Key gap:** The agent treated conversation messages only as a source for identity resolution (finding the phone number), not as a source of task requirements (what was actually requested). Existing filtering rules only reference "task instruction" text, missing that conversation content also defines binding criteria.

